{"ts": "2026-10-29T21:08:34.169268Z", "run_id": "r-20261029T2108Z-9abe", "unit": "openspec:add-web-ui-kit", "seq": 9, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-033", "target": "F-448496f9", "decision": "reject", "by": "agent", "reason": "The finding is correct and is a WCAG AA defect: the global :focus-visible outline uses --ui-color-focus #1d4ed8, and inside a toast it is drawn (2px offset) over --ui-color-toast-bg #1b1f27, a contrast of 2.46:1, below the 3:1 the requirement sets for focus (and WCAG 1.4.11 for focus indicators); theme.css has no rule that changes the outline inside a toast. Keep CONTRAST_PAIRS at its 16 pairs, which a frozen scenario pins; fix it in theme.css with an outline colour for focus inside a toast that has at least 3:1 against the toast background, for example --ui-color-toast-text (#ffffff, 16.5:1), with no new token. WHEN the Dismiss button inside a toast has keyboard focus THEN its focus outline colour has a contrast of at least 3:1 against --ui-color-toast-bg.", "text_sha256": "b30cd1f9d558451d280572f33674ec3994720c74ce66b950e79e22ddac6c7921", "answer_sha256": "0755ccd1d13421a84b867f685b1ba6ce1cb7e1cc1143ac10699e28e2e5f9f3e7", "marker": "CLAUDECODE"}
{"ts": "2026-10-29T21:08:34.181256Z", "run_id": "r-20261029T2108Z-9abe", "unit": "openspec:add-web-ui-kit", "seq": 10, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-034", "target": "H-8f5a5712", "decision": "accept", "by": "agent", "reason": "The unit can go on as it stands. Criterion C-c5c7028c was answered in Q-003 and is now judged pass: I ran the assert_accessible body of task 9.1 with axe-core 4.14.0 in Chromium, and on a page with lang and a title a labelled button returns while a button without a name fails with a message holding button-name. This round the test writer gave up only because it could not find how to import the helper, which is no defect of the unit.", "text_sha256": "6a7eec216b247ad9dc6c936aaca06cdbbcd3b387c380ad0bb4e2bed283ed2488", "answer_sha256": "c464091103d00ea1f3eee878314bd1be63ffef60477674a75eef7994392819db", "marker": "CLAUDECODE"}
{"ts": "2026-10-29T21:08:34.193244Z", "run_id": "r-20261029T2108Z-9abe", "unit": "openspec:add-web-ui-kit", "seq": 11, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-035", "target": "H-45552067", "decision": "accept", "by": "agent", "reason": "The unit can go on as it stands. Criterion C-817bfc8a, the white-on-white hover regression, is covered by its Node test (covered, passed with a red assertion in the traceability table), which checks that the toast Dismiss button keeps the toast background and text colour on hover in the theme rules. The test writer marked it not_testable only because it found no route that shows a toast; the stylesheet rule it would check is the one the Node test reads.", "text_sha256": "313eaa25b1411410a0b0899ad94675e1bb444e254fe66b22f044893e8f15ad04", "answer_sha256": "86dc093488a6eb8df740b6305f63853c1b2ec99c2dea1ac5bf5e1f93a52cb6de", "marker": "CLAUDECODE"}
